    {
      "id": "e00001",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Why chunk boundaries matter",
      "order": 1,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 1,
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        689.468017578125,
        231.56398010253906,
        702.8599853515625
      ],
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00002",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A retriever never sees a document. It sees chunks, and it can only return what a chunk contains. If the sentence that answers a question is split across two chunks, neither half may score well enough to be retrieved, and the generator is left to guess. Boundary placement is therefore a recall decision disguised as a preprocessing step.",
      "order": 2,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 1,
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        597.468017578125,
        486.19189453125,
        674.8599853515625
      ],
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00003",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Token counts in this note come from the heuristic counter, not a model tokenizer.",
      "order": 3,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 1,
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        553.468017578125,
        446.17193603515625,
        582.8599853515625
      ],
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00004",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Fixed windows",
      "order": 4,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 1,
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        525.468017578125,
        150.68399047851562,
        538.8599853515625
      ],
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00005",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The simplest strategy cuts the text every N tokens with an overlap of M tokens. It is predictable and cheap, and every chunk has the same cost to embed. It is also blind to structure: a window will happily start in the middle of a table row or end halfway through a definition.",
      "order": 5,
      "parent_id": null,
      "page": 1,
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        449.4679870605469,
        462.87591552734375,
        510.8599853515625
      ],
      "level": null,
      "md_start": null,
      "md_end": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e00006",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Page 1 of 3",
